  "schemaVersion": 21,
  "description": "Service lines (plan data) on the line a(0,1)-b(1,1)-c(2,1)-d(3,1)-e(4,1)-f(5,1)-g(6,1), dead ends at both ends. Alpha(1,0) has platform b, Beta(3,0) d, Gamma(5,0) and Delta(5,2) share f, Far(7,3) has none. createLine checks invalidName, invalidLineStops (fewer than two, or a station twice in a row), unknownStation, and gives the standard window 06:00-24:00, rate 1024 and no trains. A line's journey drives its stops out and back, turning round at the far end, from a platform of its first stop facing north, east, south or west, keeping the shortest round trip (the first among equals). Each leg takes its links x 1024 / rate minutes, rounded up; the round trip adds 1 minute at each call between the ends, out and back, and 2 at each end. Main (Alpha, Beta, Gamma) at rate 1024: four legs of 2 links, 2 minutes each, 8 + 2 + 4 = 14 minutes; at 700, 3 minutes each, 18 minutes. The most trains is the round trip / 2 (the 2-minute minimum headway), at least 1: 7, then 9. Trains in service at a level are the count set, capped by that: peak 10 runs 7, then 9; the headway is the round trip / trains, rounded up: 2, 5, 14, then 2 and 6; no trains, no headway. The service level is the service day's at that minute while the window is open: standard day low from 0, peak 420-600 and 960-1200, off-peak otherwise, low from 1260; closed outside the window (a window may close up to 1800, 06:00 the next morning). Far cannot be driven (no platform). Shared calls at two stations on one platform: no travel, 4 minutes, 2 trains. Removing e cuts Main off.",
